course: dictionary
lesson: 8104
title: A rendition is a version
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A rendition is a performance of a song, poem or piece of music, or the way it is done. When a choir sings the anthem at assembly, the words around it are the clues: «a lovely rendition of the anthem» tells you the choir performed the anthem, and they did it well.
explain: The word can also mean a version of something, like a painting copied in a new style. Check your meaning by swapping in a word like performance or version. If the sentence still makes sense, you have it.
explain: Some words have a formal meaning too. In law, «extraordinary rendition» means secretly moving a prisoner to another country for long, hard questioning. This is a grown-up use, so the context is different: it is about prisoners and countries, not songs.
fact: A rendition is a performance of a song, poem or piece of music, or the way it is done.
fact: A rendition can also be a version or translation of something.
fact: «A stirring rendition» means a powerful, moving performance.
fact: The phrases to remember are «a rendition of» and «a stirring rendition».
fact: In formal law, «extraordinary rendition» means secretly moving a prisoner to another country for long, hard questioning (US).
exercise: «The choir gave a lovely rendition of the anthem.» What is a rendition here? | A rubbish bin in the hall | A list of the choir's names | A bag of new music books | *A performance of the anthem, done well
exercise: «The artist made a rendition of her favourite painting.» What does rendition mean here? | A sale of old paintings | *A version of the painting | A shop that sells paint | A frame for the painting
exercise: «The singer gave a stirring rendition of the poem.» What does stirring suggest? | *Powerful and moving | Late and rushed | Quiet and boring | Dull and grey
test: Ella sings a rendition of a poem at the school concert. What is a rendition here? | A type of weather | A school bag | *A performance of the poem | A kind of hat
test: Which word fits? «Her French ___ of the story was lovely.» | *rendition | glum | ancient | barely
exam: Jayden reads «extraordinary rendition» in the news. What does it mean? | *Secretly moving a prisoner to another country for long, hard questioning | A school trip abroad | A bright painting of a country | A kind of song sung at a concert
